{"1-6":{"people":[{"id":"ananias-g0367g","name":"Ananias","kind":"person","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"sapphira-g4551","name":"Sapphira","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":3}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G0367","lemma":"Ἀνανίας","tr":"Ananias","gloss":"Ananias","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":11},{"base":"G3557","lemma":"νοσφίζω","tr":"nosphizō","gloss":"to embezzle","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":3},{"base":"G5574","lemma":"ψεύδομαι","tr":"pseudomai","gloss":"to lie","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"G5092","lemma":"τιμή","tr":"timē","gloss":"honor","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":41},{"base":"G5087","lemma":"τίθημι","tr":"tithēmi","gloss":"to place","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":100},{"base":"G3306","lemma":"μένω","tr":"menō","gloss":"to stay","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":118},{"base":"G2588","lemma":"καρδία","tr":"kardia","gloss":"heart","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":156},{"base":"G1135","lemma":"γυνή","tr":"gunē","gloss":"woman","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":211},{"base":"G4958","lemma":"συστέλλω","tr":"sustellō","gloss":"to wrap up","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G1634","lemma":"ἐκψύχω","tr":"ekpsuchō","gloss":"to expire","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JER","chapter":23,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"“Can a man hide in secret places where I cannot see him?” declares the LORD. “Do I not fill the heavens and the earth?” declares the LORD.","from":3},{"book":"LEV","chapter":10,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Now Aaronʼs sons Nadab and Abihu took their censers, put fire in them and added incense, and offered unauthorized fire before the LORD, contrary to His command.","from":1},{"book":"LEV","chapter":10,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Then Moses said to Aaron, “This is what the LORD meant when He said: ‘To those who come near Me I will show My holiness, and in the sight of all the people I will reveal My glory.’” But Aaron remained silent.","from":1},{"book":"ISA","chapter":29,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Woe to those who dig deep to hide their plans from the LORD. In darkness they do their works and say, “Who sees us, and who will know?”","from":3},{"book":"JHN","chapter":13,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The evening meal was underway, and the devil had already put into the heart of Judas, the son of Simon Iscariot, to betray Jesus.","from":3},{"book":"JHN","chapter":13,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And when Judas had taken the morsel, Satan entered into him. Then Jesus said to Judas, “What you are about to do, do quickly.”","from":3},{"book":"JHN","chapter":19,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So they took the body of Jesus and wrapped it in linen cloths with the spices, according to the Jewish burial custom.","from":6},{"book":"ACT","chapter":4,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"sold a field he owned, brought the money, and laid it at the apostlesʼ feet.","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":3}]},"7-11":{"people":[{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":2,"firstVerse":8}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G1627","lemma":"ἐκφέρω","tr":"ekpherō","gloss":"to bring","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"G4314","lemma":"πρός","tr":"pros","gloss":"to","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":700},{"base":"G2290","lemma":"θάπτω","tr":"thaptō","gloss":"to bury","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"G5118","lemma":"τοσοῦτος","tr":"tosoutos","gloss":"so great","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":20},{"base":"G1096","lemma":"γίνομαι","tr":"ginomai","gloss":"to be","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":668},{"base":"G4228","lemma":"πούς","tr":"pous","gloss":"foot","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":93},{"base":"G1909","lemma":"ἐπί","tr":"epi","gloss":"upon","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":885},{"base":"G4074","lemma":"Πέτρος","tr":"Petros","gloss":"Peter","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":155},{"base":"G1525","lemma":"εἰσέρχομαι","tr":"eiserchomai","gloss":"to enter","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":194},{"base":"G0435","lemma":"ἀνήρ","tr":"anēr","gloss":"man","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":216}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":5,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"On hearing these words, Ananias fell down and died. And great fear came over all who heard what had happened.","from":11},{"book":"1CO","chapter":10,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Now these things happened to them as examples and were written down as warnings for us, on whom the fulfillment of the ages has come.","from":11},{"book":"1CO","chapter":10,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"So the one who thinks he is standing firm should be careful not to fall.","from":11},{"book":"ACT","chapter":19,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"This became known to all the Jews and Greeks living in Ephesus, and fear came over all of them. So the name of the Lord Jesus was held in high honor.","from":11},{"book":"HEB","chapter":4,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Therefore, while the promise of entering His rest still stands, let us be careful that none of you be deemed to have fallen short of it.","from":11},{"book":"ACT","chapter":5,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Then Peter said, “Ananias, how is it that Satan has filled your heart to lie to the Holy Spirit and withhold some of the proceeds from the land?","from":9},{"book":"ACT","chapter":5,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Did it not belong to you before it was sold? And after it was sold, was it not at your disposal? How could you conceive such a deed in your heart? You have not lied to men, but to God!”","from":9},{"book":"1CO","chapter":10,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"We should not test Christ, as some of them did, and were killed by snakes.","from":9}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"12-16":{"people":[{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":15}],"places":[{"id":"solomon-s-portico-g4672h","name":"Solomon's Portico","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16}],"words":[{"base":"G0772","lemma":"ἀσθενής","tr":"asthenēs","gloss":"weak","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":26},{"base":"G4128","lemma":"πλῆθος","tr":"plēthos","gloss":"multitude","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":31},{"base":"G0537","lemma":"ἅπας","tr":"hapas","gloss":"all","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":33},{"base":"G2992","lemma":"λαός","tr":"laos","gloss":"a people","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":141},{"base":"G4745","lemma":"στοά","tr":"stoa","gloss":"Portico","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G1982","lemma":"ἐπισκιάζω","tr":"episkiazō","gloss":"to overshadow","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G4639","lemma":"σκιά","tr":"skia","gloss":"shadow","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"G1627","lemma":"ἐκφέρω","tr":"ekpherō","gloss":"to bring","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"G3170","lemma":"μεγαλύνω","tr":"megalunō","gloss":"to magnify","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"G4116","lemma":"πλατύς","tr":"platus","gloss":"street","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":19,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"God did extraordinary miracles through the hands of Paul,","from":12},{"book":"MAT","chapter":14,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"and begged Him just to let them touch the fringe of His cloak. And all who touched Him were healed.","from":15},{"book":"ACT","chapter":19,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"God did extraordinary miracles through the hands of Paul,","from":15},{"book":"ACT","chapter":19,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"so that even handkerchiefs and aprons that had touched him were taken to the sick, and the diseases and evil spirits left them.","from":15},{"book":"2CO","chapter":12,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"The marks of a true apostle—signs, wonders, and miracles—were performed among you with great perseverance.","from":12},{"book":"HEB","chapter":2,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"and was affirmed by God through signs, wonders, various miracles, and gifts of the Holy Spirit distributed according to His will.","from":12},{"book":"MAT","chapter":9,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"She said to herself, “If only I touch His cloak, I will be healed.”","from":15},{"book":"JHN","chapter":14,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever believes in Me will also do the works that I am doing. He will do even greater things than these, because I am going to the Father.","from":15}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"17-21":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G2411","lemma":"ἱερόν","tr":"hieros","gloss":"temple","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":70},{"base":"G0749","lemma":"ἀρχιερεύς","tr":"archiereus","gloss":"high-priest","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":122},{"base":"G4862","lemma":"σύν","tr":"sun","gloss":"with","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":128},{"base":"G3722","lemma":"ὄρθρος","tr":"orthros","gloss":"dawn","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G5084","lemma":"τήρησις","tr":"tērēsis","gloss":"jail","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G1201","lemma":"δεσμωτήριον","tr":"desmōtērion","gloss":"prison","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G1219","lemma":"δημόσιος","tr":"dēmosios","gloss":"public","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G4779","lemma":"συγκαλέω","tr":"sugkaleō","gloss":"to call together","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"G0139","lemma":"αἵρεσις","tr":"ahiresis","gloss":"sect","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"G1806","lemma":"ἐξάγω","tr":"exagō","gloss":"to lead out","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":12}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JHN","chapter":6,"verse":63,"verseEnd":63,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"The Spirit gives life; the flesh profits nothing. The words I have spoken to you are spirit and they are life.","from":20},{"book":"JHN","chapter":6,"verse":68,"verseEnd":68,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Simon Peter replied, “Lord, to whom would we go? You have the words of eternal life.","from":20},{"book":"ACT","chapter":16,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Suddenly a strong earthquake shook the foundations of the prison. At once all the doors flew open and everyoneʼs chains came loose.","from":19},{"book":"MAT","chapter":21,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"When Jesus returned to the temple courts and began to teach, the chief priests and elders of the people came up to Him. “By what authority are You doing these things?” they asked. “And who gave You this authority?”","from":20},{"book":"PSA","chapter":34,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The angel of the LORD encamps around those who fear Him, and he delivers them.","from":19},{"book":"ACT","chapter":13,"verse":45,"verseEnd":45,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"But when the Jews saw the crowds, they were filled with jealousy, and they blasphemously contradicted what Paul was saying.","from":17},{"book":"1JN","chapter":5,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"And this is that testimony: God has given us eternal life, and this life is in His Son.","from":20},{"book":"1JN","chapter":5,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Whoever has the Son has life; whoever does not have the Son of God does not have life.","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"22-32":{"people":[{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":30},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":31}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":28}],"words":[{"base":"G3980","lemma":"πειθαρχέω","tr":"peitharcheō","gloss":"to obey","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"G2476","lemma":"ἵστημι","tr":"histēmi","gloss":"to stand","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":154},{"base":"G2147","lemma":"εὑρίσκω","tr":"ehuriskō","gloss":"to find","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":176},{"base":"G4755","lemma":"στρατηγός","tr":"stratēgos","gloss":"officer","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"G1909","lemma":"ἐπί","tr":"epi","gloss":"upon","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":885},{"base":"G5257","lemma":"ὑπηρέτης","tr":"hupēretēs","gloss":"servant","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":20},{"base":"G3854","lemma":"παραγίνομαι","tr":"paraginomai","gloss":"to come","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":36},{"base":"G0518","lemma":"ἀπαγγέλλω","tr":"apangellō","gloss":"to announce","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":43},{"base":"G5438","lemma":"φυλακή","tr":"phulakē","gloss":"prison","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":47},{"base":"G0071","lemma":"ἄγω","tr":"agō","gloss":"to bring","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":68}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":15,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":32,"source":"both","text":"Then Saul said to Samuel, “I have sinned; I have transgressed the LORDʼs commandment and your instructions, because I feared the people and obeyed their voice.","from":29},{"book":"ACT","chapter":4,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":30,"source":"both","text":"But Peter and John replied, “Judge for yourselves whether it is right in Godʼs sight to listen to you rather than God.","from":29},{"book":"MRK","chapter":7,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":25,"source":"openbible","text":"They worship Me in vain; they teach as doctrine the precepts of men.’","from":29},{"book":"MRK","chapter":7,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":25,"source":"openbible","text":"He went on to say, “You neatly set aside the command of God to maintain your own tradition.","from":29},{"book":"GEN","chapter":3,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":22,"source":"both","text":"And to Adam He said: “Because you have listened to the voice of your wife and have eaten from the tree of which I commanded you not to eat, cursed is the ground because of you; through toil you will eat of it all the days of your life.","from":29},{"book":"GAL","chapter":3,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"Christ redeemed us from the curse of the law by becoming a curse for us. For it is written: “Cursed is everyone who is hung on a tree.”","from":30},{"book":"LUK","chapter":24,"verse":47,"verseEnd":47,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"and in His name repentance and forgiveness of sins will be proclaimed to all nations, beginning in Jerusalem.","from":31},{"book":"1PE","chapter":2,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"He Himself bore our sins in His body on the tree, so that we might die to sin and live to righteousness. “By His stripes you are healed.”","from":30}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"john-baptist-circle","title":"John the Baptist's Circle","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"33-42":{"people":[{"id":"gamaliel-g1059","name":"Gamaliel","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":35},{"id":"theudas-g2333","name":"Theudas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"judas-g2455k","name":"Judas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":37},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":40}],"places":[{"id":"galilee-h1551","name":"Galilee","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":37}],"words":[{"base":"G3982","lemma":"πείθω","tr":"peithō","gloss":"to persuade","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":52},{"base":"G0450","lemma":"ἀνίστημι","tr":"anistēmi","gloss":"to arise","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":107},{"base":"G0444","lemma":"ἄνθρωπος","tr":"anthrōpos","gloss":"a human","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":550},{"base":"G0868","lemma":"ἀφίστημι","tr":"aphistēmi","gloss":"to leave","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"G3686","lemma":"ὄνομα","tr":"onoma","gloss":"name","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":229},{"base":"G2647","lemma":"καταλύω","tr":"kataluō","gloss":"to destroy","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":17},{"base":"G4892","lemma":"συνέδριον","tr":"sunedrion","gloss":"council","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":22},{"base":"G0337","lemma":"ἀναιρέω","tr":"anaireō","gloss":"to kill","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":24},{"base":"G2250","lemma":"ἡμέρα","tr":"hēmera","gloss":"day","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":389},{"base":"G3745","lemma":"ὅσος","tr":"hosos","gloss":"just as","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":110}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":21,"source":"openbible","text":"There is no wisdom, no understanding, no counsel that can prevail against the LORD.","from":39},{"book":"JAS","chapter":1,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"Consider it pure joy, my brothers, when you encounter trials of many kinds,","from":41},{"book":"1PE","chapter":4,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":17,"source":"openbible","text":"But rejoice that you share in the sufferings of Christ, so that you may be overjoyed at the revelation of His glory.","from":41},{"book":"1PE","chapter":4,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":17,"source":"openbible","text":"But if you suffer as a Christian, do not be ashamed, but glorify God that you bear that name.","from":41},{"book":"ISA","chapter":46,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"I declare the end from the beginning, and from ancient times what is still to come. I say, ‘My purpose will stand, and all My good pleasure I will accomplish.’","from":39},{"book":"LUK","chapter":6,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"Blessed are you when people hate you, and when they exclude you and insult you and reject your name as evil because of the Son of Man.","from":41},{"book":"MAT","chapter":16,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"And I tell you that you are Peter, and on this rock I will build My church, and the gates of Hades will not prevail against it.","from":39},{"book":"PHP","chapter":1,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"For it has been granted to you on behalf of Christ not only to believe in Him, but also to suffer for Him,","from":41}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2}]}}